## On the job {.unnumbered}

::: callout-important
## Why this matters day to day

Regression is very likely the single most useful tool in this book for
daily work. What sets a Bayesian analysis apart is honesty about
uncertainty: you report the slope *with a credible interval*, and you
separate "how sure am I about the effect" from "how well can I predict
one specific person." Being able to make — and explain — that
distinction to a business stakeholder is a mark of a mature analysis.
:::

